  { "@type": "Question", "name": "What should a carer do when a dementia patient holds food in their mouth without swallowing?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "This is pocketing or swallowing apraxia. Try a gentle verbal prompt ('now swallow') paired with a gesture, or offer a small amount of warm water to stimulate the swallowing reflex. If it persists, refer to an SLP to assess whether the IDDSI level or feeding strategy needs adjustment. Do not use fingers or implements to forcibly remove food from the mouth." } },
