  { "@type": "Question", "name": "How early should a Parkinson's disease patient receive a swallowing assessment?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "A baseline swallowing assessment from a speech-language pathologist is recommended as early as possible after diagnosis — even before noticeable swallowing difficulties appear. This establishes an individual baseline. Annual reviews are appropriate thereafter, with earlier reassessment if symptoms worsen. Early intervention is associated with significantly slower deterioration of swallowing function." } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "How should levodopa timing be coordinated with meals?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Avoid high-protein foods (meat, fish, eggs, beans) within 30 minutes before and after each levodopa dose, as dietary protein competes with levodopa for intestinal absorption. Patients with marked On-Off fluctuations may benefit from protein redistribution — keeping breakfast and lunch low-protein and concentrating the day's protein allowance at dinner. Schedule the main meal during the On period when swallowing is safest." } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "How should mealtimes differ between On and Off periods?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "During the On period (peak medication effect, improved motor control), swallowing coordination is better — schedule the main meal here and use the highest safe IDDSI texture level. During the Off period (medication trough, tremor and rigidity worsened), move to lower IDDSI texture levels, avoid foods requiring extensive chewing, and allow substantially more time. Never rush eating during an Off period." } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "How is drooling managed in Parkinson's disease?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Drooling in Parkinson's disease occurs primarily because swallowing frequency is reduced, not because saliva production is excessive. Management includes conscious reminders to swallow every 30 seconds, maintaining good upright posture, and discussing pharmacological options such as botulinum toxin injections into the salivary glands with the attending neurologist. Accumulation of saliva increases the risk of aspiration of oral secretions." } }
];

const faqPostStrokeZhHk = [
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "中風後吞嚥困難通常多久可以恢復？", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "恢復時間因人而異。許多輕至中度患者在發病後數週至數個月內可見顯著改善，尤其大腦皮質損傷的患者恢復較快。腦幹中風的患者恢復時間通常較長，部分患者需要長期維持改良質感飲食。言語治療師可根據患者的個別情況提供更準確的預後評估。" } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "急症病房如何決定患者可否口腔進食？", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "急症中風單元護士進行初步床邊篩查（水測試或 TOR-BSST）。通過篩查的患者可以開始口腔進食。未能通過篩查的患者，由言語治療師進行正式臨床吞嚥評估，必要時安排 VFSS 或 FEES 儀器評估，才決定能否口腔進食及適合的 IDDSI 等級。" } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "照顧者在家中如何知道患者的吞嚥情況有沒有改善？", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "改善跡象包括：進食時嗆咳次數減少、進食速度加快、食量穩定增加及體重維持穩定。惡化警示包括：進食後聲音變沙啞或出現「濕聲」、發燒（可能為吸入性肺炎）、進食後反覆咳嗽。任何變化均應記錄並告知言語治療師，不應自行調整飲食等級。" } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "中風後如何預防誤吸性肺炎？", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "透過嚴格執行 IDDSI 飲食等級、維持良好口腔衛生（每餐後清潔口腔）、確保正確進食姿勢（坐直至少 90 度）及避免高風險食物，可大幅降低誤吸性肺炎的風險。中風後每餐後保持坐直至少 30–60 分鐘亦非常重要。" } }
];
const faqPostStrokeEn = [
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "How long does post-stroke dysphagia typically take to recover?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Recovery timelines vary considerably. Many patients with mild-to-moderate dysphagia see substantial improvement within weeks to a few months of onset, particularly with cortical strokes. Brainstem stroke patients generally have longer recovery trajectories, and some require long-term modified texture diets. An SLP can provide a more accurate individual prognosis based on the pattern of injury and progress." } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "How does the acute ward decide whether a patient can eat orally after stroke?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Nurses in Acute Stroke Units perform an initial bedside screen (water test or TOR-BSST). Patients who pass may begin oral feeding with monitoring. Those who fail are formally assessed by an SLP. If clinical assessment alone cannot confirm safety, VFSS or FEES is arranged. All decisions are based on formal assessment, not family or patient preference alone." } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "How can a caregiver tell whether swallowing is improving at home?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Signs of improvement include: fewer choking episodes per meal, faster eating pace, consistently increasing intake, and stable body weight. Warning signs include: voice becoming hoarse or 'wet' after eating, fever (possible aspiration pneumonia), and coughing repeatedly after meals. All changes should be documented and reported to the SLP — do not adjust the diet level independently." } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can aspiration pneumonia be prevented after stroke?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Strict adherence to the prescribed IDDSI diet level, good oral hygiene after every meal, correct eating posture (sitting upright at 90 degrees or as advised by the SLP), and avoiding high-risk foods substantially reduce the risk of aspiration pneumonia. Remaining upright for at least 30–60 minutes after each meal is also important in the post-stroke period." } }
];

const faqAlsMndZhHk = [
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "ALS 患者何時應開始調整飲食質感？", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "建議在出現吞嚥功能明顯下降的早期跡象時即開始調整，而非等到嗆咳嚴重才行動。早期跡象包括：進食時間延長、進食後明顯疲勞、偶爾輕微嗆咳，以及體重開始下降。提早調整可以讓患者以更少的精力完成進食，有助保存有限的體力，並可能延緩體重下降的速度。" } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "ALS 患者放置 PEG 後是否仍可繼續口腔進食？", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "在吞嚥仍然安全的情況下，PEG 與口腔進食可以並存。PEG 在此階段的作用是補充口腔進食攝取不足的部分，並確保藥物及液體攝取，而非取代口腔進食。隨著病情進展，口腔進食的份額會逐漸減少，但在安全前提下保留口腔進食的感官愉悅及社交意義是值得的。" } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "ALS 患者的 PEG 手術何時是最安全的時機？", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "國際及香港指引建議在用力肺活量（FVC）仍在預測值 50% 以上時進行 PEG 手術。FVC 低於 50% 時手術風險顯著增加，低於 30% 時通常不建議手術。患者應在 FVC 下降至 50% 之前，主動與醫療團隊討論 PEG 的選項及時機，避免失去安全的手術窗口。" } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "ALS 患者如何在改良質感飲食中維持足夠的能量攝取？", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "在糊狀或細碎食物中加入橄欖油（每茶匙約 40 千卡）、全脂奶粉（同時提升蛋白質）或高蛋白質粉末強化能量。選用高能量密度食材：牛油果、全脂乳製品。採用少食多餐（每日 5–6 餐）減少每次進食的負擔。定期接受營養師評估，確保達到個別的能量及蛋白質目標。" } }
];
const faqAlsMndEn = [
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "When should an ALS patient start modifying their diet texture?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Texture modification should begin at the first signs of meaningful swallowing decline — not only after severe choking episodes. Early signs include: noticeably longer mealtimes, significant post-meal fatigue, occasional mild choking on dry or fibrous textures, and the beginning of weight loss. Starting earlier conserves the patient's limited energy and may slow the rate of nutritional decline." } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can an ALS patient continue eating orally after PEG insertion?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes — as long as oral eating remains safe. When PEG is placed before oral eating is completely unsafe, it supplements rather than replaces oral intake, ensuring adequate hydration, medication and nutrition. As the disease progresses, the oral component of intake diminishes, but it can continue in parallel with PEG feeding for as long as it is safe." } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "When is the safest time for PEG insertion in ALS?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "International and Hong Kong guidelines recommend PEG insertion while forced vital capacity (FVC) remains above 50% of predicted value. Procedural risk increases substantially below 50%, and PEG is generally not recommended below 30% FVC. Patients should discuss PEG proactively with their medical team before FVC falls to 50%, to avoid losing the safe procedural window." } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "How can an ALS patient maintain adequate energy intake on a modified texture diet?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Fortify puréed and minced foods with olive oil (approximately 40 kcal per teaspoon), full-cream milk powder (boosts both protein and energy) or high-protein supplement powder. Use energy-dense ingredients: avocado, full-fat dairy products. Adopt 5–6 small meals per day to reduce the burden of each eating episode. Seek regular dietitian review to confirm individual energy and protein targets are being met." } }
];

const faqCancerDysphagiaZhHk = [
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "鼻咽癌放射治療後口乾是永久性的嗎？", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "部分口乾在治療完成後數個月至一年內可有所改善，但若唾液腺受到較高劑量照射，口乾可能是長期甚至永久性的症狀。現代強度調控放射治療（IMRT）設計上盡量保護腮腺，但由於鼻咽癌的解剖位置，完全保護並不總是可行。人工唾液及定期口腔護理可改善生活質素。" } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "頭頸癌治療後何時可以恢復正常飲食？", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "恢復的時間線因個別患者、癌症類型及治療方案而差異甚大。部分患者在治療完成後 3–6 個月內可逐步恢復接近正常的飲食，而有嚴重纖維化或牙關緊閉的患者可能長期需要改良質感飲食。言語治療師定期進行 VFSS 評估，可客觀追蹤進展並作出適時的飲食等級調整建議。" } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "放射治療後的牙關緊閉可以治療嗎？", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "牙關緊閉的治療以早期介入及持續訓練為主。TheraBite 等張口訓練器材配合規律的張口運動，在部分患者中可見到功能改善。最重要的是在治療期間或治療完成後盡快開始預防性張口運動，避免等到嚴重攣縮才介入。手術介入在嚴重個案中有時考慮，但效果不一。" } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "鼻咽癌治療後何時需要再進行 VFSS 評估？", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "建議在治療完成後 3–6 個月進行首次 VFSS 評估，此後至少每年複查一次。以下情況應立即安排評估：吞嚥困難明顯加重、出現吞嚥疼痛、體重急速下降、反覆發燒（可能為吸入性肺炎），或主觀感覺吞嚥功能與之前不同。晚期纖維化可在治療後數年才顯現，持續監察至關重要。" } }
];
const faqCancerDysphagiaEn = [
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "Is xerostomia after NPC radiotherapy permanent?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Some degree of saliva recovery can occur in the months to one year after treatment, but if the salivary glands received a high radiation dose, xerostomia may be a long-term or permanent condition. Modern IMRT techniques aim to spare the parotid glands, but complete sparing is not always achievable given NPC anatomy. Artificial saliva and rigorous oral hygiene can substantially improve quality of life." } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "When can a head and neck cancer patient return to a normal diet?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The timeline varies considerably depending on the individual patient, cancer type and treatment regimen. Some patients gradually resume a near-normal diet within 3–6 months of completing treatment, while those with significant fibrosis or trismus may require long-term modified texture diets. Regular VFSS assessment by the SLP provides objective data to guide diet level progression." } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can trismus (restricted mouth opening) after radiotherapy be treated?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The primary approach is early and sustained jaw-stretching exercises, using purpose-designed devices such as TheraBite. With consistent effort, functional improvement is possible in many patients. The most important principle is to begin prophylactic jaw exercises during or immediately after radiotherapy — not only after severe contracture has developed. Surgical intervention is occasionally considered for severe cases." } },
  { "@type": "Question", "name": "When should post-NPC treatment VFSS reassessment be arranged?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The first VFSS evaluation is recommended 3–6 months after treatment completion, then at minimum annual review. Immediate reassessment should be arranged if swallowing noticeably worsens, if swallowing becomes painful, if unexplained weight loss occurs, if recurrent fever suggests aspiration pneumonia, or if the patient subjectively notices a change. Late fibrosis can manifest years after treatment, making continued monitoring essential." } }
];

